## Where to look
- `results/logbook.md` — per-experiment narrative detail; grep or read a slice for one old experiment.
- `results/scoreboard.tsv` — the numeric series, one row per experiment.
- `results/checks_<NN>.json` — what the runner mechanically checked for one experiment, and what it
  could not check. Read it after your run: a `fail` is a bug or a discovery and is yours to explain,
  and an `unavailable` names in its `needs` field exactly what this campaign would have to supply to
  make that check real. Neither is a passed check.
- `configs/loop.json` `campaign` — what kind of campaign this is: whether a prediction must carry a
  numeric range, and whether a win is judged against a replicate spread or a numerical tolerance.
